msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:87
msgid "HTTP CONNECT method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:89
msgid "The meaning of the `CONNECT` method from RFC 7231, section 4.3.6:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:91
msgid ""
"The CONNECT method requests that the recipient establish a tunnel to the "
"destination origin server identified by the request-target and, if "
"successful, thereafter restrict its behavior to blind forwarding of "
"packets, in both directions, until the tunnel is closed.  Tunnels are "
"commonly used to create an end-to-end virtual connection, through one or "
"more proxies, which can then be secured using TLS (Transport Layer "
"Security, [RFC5246])."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:99
msgid ""
"In Node.js, these request objects come from the `'connect'` event on the "
"HTTP server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:102
msgid ""
"When this module is used on a HTTP `CONNECT` request, the request is "
"considered \"finished\" immediately, **due to limitations in the Node.js "
"interface**. This means if the `CONNECT` request contains a request "
"entity, the request will be considered \"finished\" even before it has "
"been read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:107
msgid ""
"There is no such thing as a response object to a `CONNECT` request in "
"Node.js, so there is no support for one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:110
msgid "HTTP Upgrade request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:112
msgid "The meaning of the `Upgrade` header from RFC 7230, section 6.1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:114
msgid ""
"The \"Upgrade\" header field is intended to provide a simple mechanism "
"for transitioning from HTTP/1.1 to some other protocol on the same "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:118
msgid ""
"In Node.js, these request objects come from the `'upgrade'` event on the "
"HTTP server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:121
msgid ""
"When this module is used on a HTTP request with an `Upgrade` header, the "
"request is considered \"finished\" immediately, **due to limitations in "
"the Node.js interface**. This means if the `Upgrade` request contains a "
"request entity, the request will be considered \"finished\" even before "
"it has been read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/on-finished_README.md:127
msgid ""
"There is no such thing as a response object to a `Upgrade` request in "
"Node.js, so there is no support for one."
msgstr ""

